{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he said: Let there not now be wrath, etc.</b> The reason he feared wrath is that he wished that He would shield, and he feared the Creator's rigor, and said ״אַל יִחַר״ etc. And he was precise to say <b>na</b> — meaning: for what he says this time, that he asks that his merit may shield — perhaps thirty may be found, that the Master shields for one population and Abraham for one population."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:13.071905144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}